      "card_ids": ["C21"]
    },
    {
      "family": "associated_nonvoting_records",
      "applicability": "not_applicable",
      "direction": "neutral_or_unclear",
      "decision_effect": "no_change",
      "card_ids": ["C16", "C22", "C25", "C27"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct oral bioavailability measurement is available for the query molecule itself.",
    "No record card exactly matches a quaternary pyridinium carbamate; transfer from physostigmine and BMS-187745 is indirect.",
    "First-pass carbamate hydrolysis and possible active or paracellular absorption of the quaternary ammonium are not characterized in the supplied records.",
    "The property tool reports neutral fraction = 1 despite the formal positive charge in the SMILES, adding uncertainty to the physicochemical prior.",
    "The near-threshold rat value for methyl parathion (~20%) and the mismatched PMF relative-comparison card limit directness of the L2 context."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Predicted low (F < 20%) because the query is a permanently charged quaternary pyridinium carbamate; the closest carbamate context (physostigmine) reports poor oral bioavailability, a charged polar context (BMS-187745) reports 2.6% absolute F, and multiple related low-F contexts (tilidine, agomelatine, apocynin, aniracetam) remain below 20%. New L2 records reinforce this direction; the only near-threshold rat value (methyl parathion ~20%) is not transferable enough to overturn."
}

